I have a comprehensive picture. Here are my findings.

## Summary

This is a Spring PetClinic variant built on the OfficeFloor framework. The `POST /api/owners` flow is defined declaratively in a YAML file that chains small single-purpose "function" classes. Dates are represented as `java.time.LocalDate` throughout (entity, functions, mapper). Key finding: a business-day roll is expected by tests but is NOT implemented in production — see item 5.

---

### 1. Registration date set/defaulted

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java`
```java
15  public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
16      if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
17          owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
18      }
19  }
```
- If the request body supplied a `registrationDate` it is left untouched; otherwise it defaults to `LocalDate.now()` (raw server date, no weekend/holiday adjustment).
- Runs as the `defaultRegistrationDate` step in `owners.POST.yml` (after `assignHousehold`, before `assignCustomerCode`).

Field on entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` lines 56-57 (`@Column(name = "registration_date") private LocalDate registrationDate;`), getter/setter lines 103-109.

OpenAPI schema: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2044-2049 (`format: date`, "Defaults to the server's current date when omitted").

DB column `registration_date DATE` in all four schemas: `db/h2/schema.sql:39`, `db/postgres/schema.sql:34`, `db/mysql/schema.sql:36`, `db/hsqldb/schema.sql:46`.

### 2. Membership number generation (year segment from registration date)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` lines 44-54:
```java
47  default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {
48      String customerCode = owner.getCustomerCode();
49      LocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
50      if (customerCode == null || registrationDate == null) {
51          return null;
52      }
53      return String.format("%s-M%02d", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100);
54  }
```
- Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` (last two digits of the registration year), e.g. `SPR-SMI-0007-M26`. Computed lazily during DTO mapping (`toOwnerDto`, line 25 `@Mapping`), not persisted.
- Related `customerCode` (the prefix of the membership number) is generated separately:
